krs 1
# The generic synthesis by Yosys of a lane that GHDL wrote as Verilog, as a script that Yosys reads one command to a
# line (`yosys -s`). The format is the comment at the head of ptx.krs.
#
# The script is the own passes of synth, made lighter. Each opt is `opt -fast`, in place of the full `opt` and
# `opt -full` of synth, and the script leaves out `fsm` and `share`. Thus the cost read is the lane as written, with its
# state register as the process holds it, and each operation as its own operator.
#
# The passes give the netlist that the cost comes from. That is the memories that `memory -nomap` infers before the
# fine stage maps them to flops, and the read ports that it registers (`merging output FF`). Then the cells that `stat`
# counts, and the longest path that `ltp` walks (`(length=`).
ruleset yosys
toolchain yosys
header read_source

# the Verilog GHDL wrote
form read_source source = read_verilog {source}\n
# the hierarchy of the design from its top, its processes as cells, and its arithmetic and memories as coarse cells
form coarse top = hierarchy -check -top {top}\nproc\nopt_expr\nopt_clean\nopt -fast -nodffe -nosdff\nwreduce\npeepopt\nopt_clean\nalumacc\nopt -fast\nmemory -nomap\nopt_clean\n
# the statistics of the coarse netlist, written quietly to a log while its memories are still cells
form memories log = tee -q -o {log} stat\n
# the memories mapped to flops, the coarse cells to gates, and the gates to a netlist by the fast script of abc. That
# script folds the constants of the gates itself, thus no `opt` runs between the maps
form fine = memory_map\ntechmap\nabc -fast\nopt -fast\n
# the cells of the netlist and its longest path, with the flops cut
form measure = stat\nltp -noff\n
